+
+## Forward V15: one original Resume and Stop from open
+
+This privately prepared increment retains V14's accepted closed-lab behavior
+and adds one path. The installed recorder acquires its original fence while
+paused. The actual control session opens the source at position three with
+an original Resume that names the exact head and held UUID/revision. The
+original reserved Stop then names that Resume's original Command SHA and
+stops from open at position four. The earlier paused Stop paths remain.
+
+The broker still uses the existing trusted owner and one private EXECUTE
+grant. Its internal Boolean enables an extra row lock only for Resume.
+After locking the package and actual caller, it locks the recorder derived
+from the held genesis within the same scope. The sealed native owner still
+has anchor SELECT and broker EXECUTE, without anchor DML. Fresh Resume
+authenticates the actual control and independently resolves the recorder
+from the locked binding and held manifest. The deferred guard revalidates
+those facts under the locks and derives the same exact dependency and
+identity set. The public getter retains its original read-authority path and
+verifies historical writers and clocks from sealed inputs. Stop takes no
+recorder row lock or live fence check.
+
+Resume keeps the original fence ID, acquisition epoch and revision. Its own
+single identity is a new control_action_id. The independent getter checks
+historical Resume and Stop body, dependency and result shapes, exact scoped
+role association, committed journal links and full scalar encoding. The
+receipt holds separate final-function and commit-processing observations.
+For Resume they fall within the original live fence. The cost envelope
+charges a retained active UUID for Resume, and the existing budget keeps
+the full terminal reserve. The policy descriptor, owner inventory count,
+and ordinary writer, readiness and outer time limits are preserved.
+
+The Resume Result has six direct pins and the getter closure has ten. The
+open Stop Result has six direct pins and the getter closure has thirteen.
+Previous-head and prior-control point to the same Resume Command, which is
+one pin. The selected four-operation witness expects 56 retained rows,
+54 logical writes and 108 logical keys, and 58 row and 120 key touches
+including staging. Source-authored tests remain pending native execution.
+
+Five added methods cover the exact lifecycle and independently observed
+accounting, closed actor/command/identity/mode refusals, a recorder binding
+lock with rollback and open Stop independence, changed recorder revalidation,
+and real expiry at late COMMIT and fresh Resume with original Stop preserved.
+The expiry case uses one owned read scheduled relative to the real retained
+deadline. All 29 prior test IDs are retained. The unsupported-kind loop no
+longer lists Resume and the existing broker ACL probe checks the changed
+signature with both flags.
+
+V15 does not implement renew or another transition. The distinct seven-pin
+Stop, position-reserve witness, empirical capacity and dedicated production
+broker owner remain separate. Source stays in the private review candidate.
